WEBVTT

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:14.300
Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:22.680
aoku nemuru mizu no hoshi ni sotto

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:22.680
Kissing softly the star of water that sleeps in blue,

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:31.410
kuchizuke shite inochi no hi wo tomosu hito yo

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:31.410
A person who lights the fire of life,

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:36.300
toki to iu kin'iro no sazanami wa

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:36.300
The time, the golden ripple,

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:45.070
oozora no kuchibiru ni umareta toiki ne

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:45.070
is a sigh from the lips of the sky,

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:49.300
kokoro ni uzumoreta

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:49.300
The stars of kindness...

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.270
yasashisa no hoshitachi ga

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.270
...buried in heart flame up...

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:56.440
honoo age yobiau

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:56.440
...and call to each other,

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:03.430
namima sasurau nanpasen no you ni

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:03.430
Like wrecked ships wandering on the waves...

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:08.870
mou nakanaide ima

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:08.870
Don't cry, any more,

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:16.240
anata wo sagashite iru hito ga iru kara

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:16.240
because now there is a person looking for you,

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.970
omae ni aitai yo to

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.970
Dying to see you...

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:39.940
Kamille rescued Four from
the Titans' base in Kilimanjaro.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:43.970
However, Four was unable to
quit piloting the Psyco Gundam.

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:48.600
Four was held in Kamille's arms...

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:52.100
...never fully realizing
the tragedy of her fate.

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:57.130
The Day of Dakar

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:09.390
We've confirmed
the enemy Garuda's position!

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:10.730
Where is it?!

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:12.770
It's descending above the African continent!

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:15.100
It seems to be taking a ballistic trajectory.

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:18.140
- Where will it land?!
- Can't quite tell yet.

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:20.680
I know! It has to be Dakar!

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:23.440
That's the only place they
could logically be going.

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:25.440
Direct the Melord to Dakar!

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:29.220
That's a leased territory held by the
Federation! We need authorization to enter.

00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:33.120
We have orders from His Excellency
Jamitov to hunt down Karaba!

00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:34.990
There's no reason to hesitate!

00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:35.960
Yes, sir!

00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:56.010
You're not serving as a mobile suit pilot
in this next operation, Lieutenant.

00:02:56.380 --> 00:03:00.480
Yes, I know that, but I can't help
worrying about the mobile suits.

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:03.650
I understand how you feel,
but we're almost in Dakar.

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:06.150
And Karaba?

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:08.320
Some of our members have
infiltrated the general assembly.

00:03:08.690 --> 00:03:10.960
However, this all depends on you.

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:15.260
Unlike the other pilots,
we have no replacement for you.

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:16.990
I know.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:23.610
Kamille.

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:25.110
Mr. Amuro.

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:26.700
Can you fight?

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:28.510
I feel better when I'm moving.

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:32.240
And I'm well aware that crying about it
won't bring Four back.

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:33.980
That's important to know.

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:37.180
It took both Char and myself
seven years to understand that.

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:42.850
But I still have trouble understanding
why I must fight.

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:45.350
Fighting is meaningless in itself.

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:48.760
But humanity has developed its history
by continued fighting.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.860
Without it, mankind would
have been extinct.

00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:56.370
Has Miss Beltorchika changed
because she came to that realization?

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:57.640
Why do you ask?

00:03:57.810 --> 00:04:00.070
To go to Dakar for the preparations...

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:02.270
...is something she wouldn't have done
in the past.

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:04.780
She's an Oldtype.

00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:07.720
She forgets about the agony of the past,
and jumps into the next thing.

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:11.220
How much longer will humans
be like that, I wonder.

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:16.890
I'm glad it's you giving me a ride.

00:04:17.260 --> 00:04:19.690
Otherwise I would easily
get shot down.

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:21.630
You should have no reason
to hesitate.

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:24.830
You're the only one in the A.E.U.G.
capable of leading the organization.

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:29.100
Even though I'm still unable
to make a decision on my own future?

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:35.710
The general public is always looking
for a hero.

00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:38.410
So you're telling me
to play the role of a clown.

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:41.180
All I'm saying is it's your turn
to take center stage.

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:43.820
The script hasn't been rewritten
or anything.

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:45.920
Amuro.

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:49.080
People change. It's natural.

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:58.030
We've also taken over the communication
facilities over there.

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:00.170
Including the local staff?

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:02.100
We removed any opposition.

00:05:02.170 --> 00:05:03.040
I see.

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:05.070
Then all that's left is to wait for him.

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:08.970
Mr. Luio Woomin is looking
forward to today's TV broadcast.

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:16.120
Sorry, but there's no entrance past here.

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:18.480
Take care of the preparations.

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:21.420
Right. And you make sure
you get that item.

00:05:21.490 --> 00:05:22.460
Okay.

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:32.560
Karen Russel?

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:33.830
You're with the television crew?

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:35.140
Yes.

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:38.470
Shopping? But you should be able to get
practically everything here.

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:40.780
The camera plug is busted.

00:05:41.010 --> 00:05:43.140
I'm sorry, but I can't let you through.

00:05:43.310 --> 00:05:46.150
Why not? I thought reporters had access.

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:47.780
These are orders from above.

00:05:47.850 --> 00:05:48.870
Come on.

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:53.510
Why not just say you can't get coverage of
the assembly because of jammed airwaves...

00:05:53.590 --> 00:05:54.750
...like always?

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:59.160
Although... that doesn't make sense
since you're using fiber optics.

00:06:00.930 --> 00:06:03.330
What'll I do? I really need it.

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:06.690
If you're that desperate,
perhaps we can figure out a way...

00:06:06.770 --> 00:06:08.030
...if you know what I mean.

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:09.870
Stop right there before you screw up.

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:11.570
Who the hell are you?!

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:14.270
Is that the only way you can
ask a girl for a date?

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:16.940
Go on.

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:19.510
How dare you interfere
with our fun!

00:06:21.050 --> 00:06:22.680
Stop picking on the weak!

00:06:22.790 --> 00:06:24.480
- You're asking for it!
- Stop it!

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:26.850
- This guy's with the Titans!
- Titans?!

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:30.380
Would you mind giving me a ride
to the Dakar Base?

00:06:30.460 --> 00:06:32.020
N-Not at all.

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:38.700
The Federation's soldiers
aren't all like that.

00:06:39.340 --> 00:06:41.200
You seem sure about that,
Lieutenant Addis.

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:44.840
At least, there aren't any guys
like that in the Titans.

00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:47.380
Wouldn't it be wonderful
if everyone were like you?

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:49.380
This is an era of confusion.

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:52.410
During times like these, we must
have a righteous armed force...

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:54.450
...that can properly manage everything.

00:06:55.450 --> 00:06:56.920
Whose words are those?

00:06:58.760 --> 00:07:00.880
Well, you didn't write
that phrase yourself, did you?

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:02.750
They're words of His Excellency Jamitov.

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:06.930
This is the place, right?

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:09.060
Thank you.

00:07:09.630 --> 00:07:11.730
I wish I could talk with you
a little longer.

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:14.330
If you're up to it...

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:17.810
...why don't you check out
my coverage of the assembly?

00:07:18.210 --> 00:07:19.230
For sure.

00:07:19.310 --> 00:07:22.300
Give me your comments after you see it.

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:24.350
We'll meet again.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:36.590
Targeted landing point confirmed!

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:38.590
Okay, begin descent!

00:07:40.930 --> 00:07:42.920
Let's hope we can avoid all the missiles.

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:44.430
I'm praying that we will.

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:48.200
Kamille! Let's do it!

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:58.440
Mobile suits have begun to descend
from the skies of Dakar!

00:07:58.850 --> 00:08:01.010
Transmit the friend-or-foe
I.D. signal...

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:02.570
- ...or else we'll be shot down!
- Yes, sir!

00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:04.020
Darn!

00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:06.780
Dakar's one place where we lack
a sufficient battle strength!

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:10.260
The enemy wants to throw Dakar
into confusion for political purposes!

00:08:10.330 --> 00:08:13.780
Leave the ground defense
to the Dakar garrison!

00:08:14.330 --> 00:08:15.630
Lieutenant Addis!

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:19.130
You're going out even with
a fractured shoulder bone?

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:20.560
I can fight!

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:24.000
We're not so short of combatants that
we need to send out injured pilots!

00:08:24.070 --> 00:08:24.900
Stay behind!

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:38.780
We'll break up so the enemy
can't tell where we're landing!

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:41.190
- Avoid meaningless battles!
- <i>Roger.</i>

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:07.450
Be careful, Beltorchika!

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:10.120
You, too!

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:17.850
Now you only need
to get onto the podium.

00:09:18.060 --> 00:09:20.030
I'm impressed that you got all this
in place so quickly.

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:21.850
We owe it all to the Luio Family.

00:09:22.030 --> 00:09:24.730
Mr. Luio has a strong influence
over some of the assembly members.

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:31.510
A mobile suit team?!

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:33.540
Not until Char finishes his speech!

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:37.840
<i>We'll pause for a moment.</i>

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:40.440
<i>We have word on an unidentified craft</i>
<i>moving in.</i>

00:09:40.520 --> 00:09:41.450
<i>Any objections?</i>

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:42.250
Not at all!

00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:45.850
This should have been decided
a lot sooner, Mr. Speaker!

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:48.450
- How close is the A.E.U.G.?!
- I hope we're still safe!

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:49.550
Close the meeting now!

00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:51.560
This isn't good.

00:09:53.930 --> 00:09:54.730
Lieutenant!

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:56.590
Do not close the meeting!

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:58.330
I'd like to take over for a moment!

00:09:58.600 --> 00:10:00.760
- Unauthorized persons are...!
- Don't move!

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:03.430
- We'll be using this stage!
- Bastards!

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:05.210
We're from the A. E. U.G.!

00:10:05.270 --> 00:10:07.740
- What the hell?!
- Shut up and let him speak!

00:10:07.940 --> 00:10:09.640
<i>I start by asking all assembly members...</i>

00:10:09.710 --> 00:10:12.310
<i>...and Federation citizens</i>
<i>watching this broadcast...</i>

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:14.910
<i>...to forgive me for</i>
<i>this sudden act of insolence.</i>

00:10:16.950 --> 00:10:20.180
<i>I am Lieutenant Quattro Bajeena</i>
<i>of the A.E.U.G..</i>

00:10:20.790 --> 00:10:23.350
Go home! Stop the broadcast!

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:24.860
Are you taking over
this general assembly?!

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:25.830
I won't be listening!

00:10:25.900 --> 00:10:27.920
Camera, focus in on them!

00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:31.330
<i>There's one thing I must disclose</i>
<i>before I begin.</i>

00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:36.070
<i>I am the man previously referred to</i>
<i>as Char Aznable.</i>

00:10:37.470 --> 00:10:39.810
Is he Zeon's Red Comet?

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:45.940
<i>I want to talk to you as one</i>
<i>who bears the aspirations of Zeon.</i>

00:10:46.820 --> 00:10:50.250
<i>Needless to say, not as Char</i>
<i>of the Principality of Zeon...</i>

00:10:50.320 --> 00:10:52.150
<i>...but as the son of Zeon Deikun.</i>

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:55.020
He's the son of Zeon Deikun?!

00:10:55.090 --> 00:10:56.150
Damn the A.E.U.G.!

00:10:56.230 --> 00:10:57.820
Who the hell does he think he is?!

00:10:58.330 --> 00:11:02.660
<i>The will of Zeon Deikun is different</i>
<i>from that of the greedy Zabi Family.</i>

00:11:02.900 --> 00:11:04.490
<i>Zeon Deikun did not...</i>

00:11:04.570 --> 00:11:07.540
- <i>...build the Principality of Zeon!</i>
- Hey, that woman.

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:08.930
<i>Considering the present reality...</i>

00:11:09.010 --> 00:11:12.100
<i>...where the Titans do as they please</i>
<i>with the Earth Federation Forces...</i>

00:11:12.170 --> 00:11:14.840
<i>...it's evident the Titans are even more</i>
<i>malicious than the Zabi Family.</i>

00:11:14.910 --> 00:11:16.000
Blast him!

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:17.980
<i>All units, level one battle stations!</i>

00:11:18.480 --> 00:11:21.140
<i>An unknown aircraft</i>
<i>has entered the battle air zone!</i>

00:11:21.350 --> 00:11:23.250
<i>People went to space...</i>

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:26.980
<i>...so that Earth would not collapse</i>
<i>under the weight of humans.</i>

00:11:27.190 --> 00:11:29.090
<i>And then, the people who went to space...</i>

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:32.660
<i>...continued to expand</i>
<i>their living space.</i>

00:11:32.730 --> 00:11:33.660
<i>As a result...</i>

00:11:33.730 --> 00:11:36.660
<i>...history shows that humans wrongfully</i>
<i>believed they enhanced...</i>

00:11:36.730 --> 00:11:39.460
<i>...the powers of humanity itself,</i>
<i>creating forces like the Zabi Family.</i>

00:11:39.540 --> 00:11:40.500
<i>That's very unfortunate.</i>

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:43.840
<i>We mustn't repeat that history.</i>

00:11:51.780 --> 00:11:52.610
Enemies!

00:11:55.380 --> 00:11:56.680
Asshimars again!

00:12:14.400 --> 00:12:15.530
It's escaping?!

00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:18.700
No, they're trying to buy more time
for that broadcast.

00:12:22.350 --> 00:12:23.900
<i>Why can't humans believe...</i>

00:12:23.980 --> 00:12:27.880
<i>...that they could expand their capacities</i>
<i>by going to space?</i>

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:30.350
The Titans are doing that!

00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:34.290
<i>I am saying we humans</i>
<i>must not pollute Earth!</i>

00:12:34.360 --> 00:12:38.490
<i>The Titans are comprised of people</i>
<i>whose souls are pulled by Earth...</i>

00:12:38.560 --> 00:12:40.390
<i>...and are about to devour it!</i>

00:12:40.760 --> 00:12:42.560
Did you find out where
their communications facilities are?!

00:12:42.930 --> 00:12:44.520
<i>North of the assembly hall!</i>

00:12:44.600 --> 00:12:45.530
Right!

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:47.690
Okay, we'll destroy the fiber optic
communication facilities!

00:12:54.940 --> 00:12:56.640
Mike, we'll go separately.

00:12:56.710 --> 00:13:00.110
We're above the city.
Be careful with your rifle!

00:13:00.180 --> 00:13:01.150
<i>Roger!</i>

00:13:05.290 --> 00:13:07.780
This isn't the time to be fighting!

00:13:14.300 --> 00:13:17.090
- How far do you plan to run!
- Stop! I don't intend to fight!

00:13:17.170 --> 00:13:18.690
What?!

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:24.100
I'll fire!

00:13:29.040 --> 00:13:31.010
Don't fall to the city
with that minimal damage!

00:13:31.550 --> 00:13:33.340
Mike, have you been hit?!

00:13:33.420 --> 00:13:34.850
That bastard!

00:13:41.090 --> 00:13:42.750
He won't make it!

00:13:51.230 --> 00:13:52.220
I can't do it!

00:13:59.740 --> 00:14:01.540
Why did you save me?!

00:14:01.940 --> 00:14:03.280
I have no intention of attacking.

00:14:03.350 --> 00:14:05.470
I just want the speech to continue!

00:14:05.550 --> 00:14:06.980
You're full of it!

00:14:09.390 --> 00:14:10.440
Oh, no!

00:14:10.520 --> 00:14:12.610
There's a different team
headed toward the assembly hall!

00:14:16.360 --> 00:14:18.260
Wait, I'm not finished talking to you!

00:14:18.660 --> 00:14:21.490
Listen to the assembly meeting broadcast!
Then you'll understand!

00:14:24.870 --> 00:14:26.330
Assembly meeting broadcast?

00:14:26.400 --> 00:14:27.390
What's the big deal?

00:14:29.210 --> 00:14:33.610
<i>For the longest time, people have played</i>
<i>in this cradle called Earth.</i>

00:14:33.940 --> 00:14:39.540
<i>However, the time has arrived</i>
<i>for humanity to leave this nest.</i>

00:14:40.280 --> 00:14:42.750
<i>Then why, during this important time...</i>

00:14:42.820 --> 00:14:45.690
<i>...must humanity fight against each other,</i>
<i>and further pollute Earth?!</i>

00:14:49.490 --> 00:14:52.430
<i>Earth must be restored to</i>
<i>its natural state as a cradle...</i>

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:54.460
<i>...and humans must establish themselves</i>
<i>in space.</i>

00:14:55.130 --> 00:14:57.860
<i>Otherwise, Earth will no longer be</i>
<i>a "planet of water"!</i>

00:15:03.240 --> 00:15:04.260
A Byalant?!

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:06.070
Where's it going?!

00:15:06.510 --> 00:15:07.770
To attack the communications base?!

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:12.210
<i>Even this city of Dakar is about to be</i>
<i>engulfed by the desert!</i>

00:15:12.780 --> 00:15:14.720
<i>This is how exhausted the Earth is!</i>

00:15:15.520 --> 00:15:18.450
The assembly members
are being drawn to his speech.

00:15:19.360 --> 00:15:20.320
What was that?!

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:22.360
<i>Mobile suits are</i>
<i>approaching from the sky.</i>

00:15:22.420 --> 00:15:24.190
Do we have a working camera out there?

00:15:24.260 --> 00:15:26.230
<i>Not one!</i>

00:15:26.960 --> 00:15:28.360
- Come with me!
- Where?

00:15:28.430 --> 00:15:29.400
Outside!

00:15:29.870 --> 00:15:31.560
Shoot the battle going on outside!

00:15:31.630 --> 00:15:33.600
We'll show just how vicious
the Titans are!

00:15:34.540 --> 00:15:36.100
I won't let you interfere!

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:43.550
Mr. Amuro!

00:15:47.980 --> 00:15:49.110
The Gundam's arrived!

00:15:51.790 --> 00:15:52.690
There!

00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:10.870
The Titans are trying to destroy
the communications facility.

00:16:10.940 --> 00:16:14.930
<i>Right now, each one of us would like</i>
<i>to see this Earth remain beautiful.</i>

00:16:16.610 --> 00:16:20.570
<i>Then there's no way we should be</i>
<i>clinging to Earth like parasites...</i>

00:16:20.650 --> 00:16:22.980
<i>...just to satisfy our own desires!</i>

00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:35.560
The Dijeh... that's Amuro.

00:16:40.270 --> 00:16:42.200
The battle's getting awfully close!

00:16:42.270 --> 00:16:43.330
It's the A.E.U.G.!

00:16:43.410 --> 00:16:45.870
If the Titans didn't start it,
the A.E.U.G. would not retaliate!

00:16:46.080 --> 00:16:48.040
- Come on!
- I... can't stand...!

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:49.270
Hand it over!

00:16:51.010 --> 00:16:53.310
Listen! Show this image!

00:16:59.720 --> 00:17:03.420
<i>As we speak, the Titans have decided to</i>
<i>begin a battle regardless of this gathering.</i>

00:17:03.690 --> 00:17:06.090
<i>See the tyrannical actions</i>
<i>they're taking!</i>

00:17:06.160 --> 00:17:08.650
<i>They've emerged from the previous</i>
<i>Earth Federation Forces...</i>

00:17:08.730 --> 00:17:11.060
<i>...and label any opponents as evil.</i>

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:12.860
<i>But that in itself is evil...</i>

00:17:12.940 --> 00:17:15.060
<i>...and we can say that it's the cause</i>
<i>of humanity's decline!</i>

00:17:17.140 --> 00:17:18.300
I don't understand.

00:17:18.370 --> 00:17:20.100
What's right or wrong?

00:17:20.410 --> 00:17:21.670
I won't let you go!

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:27.010
Now!
Destroy the communications facilities!

00:17:27.950 --> 00:17:28.920
Oh, no!

00:17:31.490 --> 00:17:32.850
We won't make it in time!

00:17:34.220 --> 00:17:35.950
We mustn't interrupt this broadcast!

00:17:42.400 --> 00:17:44.830
I see we have a traitor
within our own allied forces!

00:17:45.900 --> 00:17:47.370
I won't let you!

00:17:57.510 --> 00:17:58.740
The Titans.

00:17:58.810 --> 00:18:02.110
They might be the kind of group
described in the broadcast.

00:18:05.750 --> 00:18:07.220
Okay!

00:18:09.490 --> 00:18:11.820
I cannot allow it to explode in the city.

00:18:15.130 --> 00:18:16.890
Damn!

00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:18.630
Damn you!

00:18:18.700 --> 00:18:20.790
It's your own fault for being fooled.

00:18:20.870 --> 00:18:22.340
You're dying with me.

00:18:25.210 --> 00:18:27.370
That's clumsy of you, Kamille.

00:18:27.440 --> 00:18:30.440
I didn't expect to part with you here.

00:18:32.180 --> 00:18:33.810
Why are you trying to wreck
the general assembly?!

00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:34.850
What?!

00:18:35.020 --> 00:18:38.110
If the Titans are correct, it should
be proven at the general assembly!

00:18:38.190 --> 00:18:39.620
Which unit are you from?!

00:18:39.860 --> 00:18:41.320
The Titans are all about power!

00:18:41.390 --> 00:18:43.690
Those who have power will
conquer everything!

00:18:45.390 --> 00:18:46.880
Stop it!

00:18:55.800 --> 00:18:58.400
<i>I'm sure those of you watching</i>
<i>television have realized...</i>

00:18:58.470 --> 00:19:00.570
<i>...this is how the Titans</i>
<i>go about their business!</i>

00:19:00.640 --> 00:19:03.670
<i>Yes, we were wrong to take over</i>
<i>the general assembly by force.</i>

00:19:03.750 --> 00:19:07.110
<i>However, the Titans are trying to</i>
<i>destroy this place...</i>

00:19:07.180 --> 00:19:10.710
<i>...even though there are assembly members</i>
<i>who are their allies here, too!</i>

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:14.020
How dare you get in my way!

00:19:19.130 --> 00:19:20.100
What are you doing?!

00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:24.430
<i>We have orders to stop fighting!</i>
<i>This battle is being shown on television!</i>

00:19:24.500 --> 00:19:25.330
What?!

00:19:25.400 --> 00:19:28.860
<i>We cannot have the citizens</i>
<i>of the Federation turn against us!</i>

00:19:28.940 --> 00:19:31.870
<i>These are orders from above!</i>
<i>Please withdraw!</i>

00:19:31.940 --> 00:19:34.270
But we're playing right into
the A.E.U.G.'s hand!

00:19:34.340 --> 00:19:35.940
Are you okay with that?!

00:19:37.180 --> 00:19:38.440
Are they fighting in the city?!

00:19:38.510 --> 00:19:40.140
The Titans are doing such awful things!

00:19:40.220 --> 00:19:42.840
- It's happening in Dakar.
- The Titans are a group of murderers.

00:19:42.920 --> 00:19:46.450
You're also a murderer.
We're all murderers.

00:19:46.520 --> 00:19:48.110
We live on licking each other's wounds...

00:19:48.190 --> 00:19:49.780
...and then kill each other.

00:19:49.860 --> 00:19:51.220
He's in love with himself.

00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:55.790
<i>The airwaves are jammed</i>
<i>with irregular waves.</i>

00:19:55.860 --> 00:19:58.490
<i>We'll be going off the air temporarily.</i>

00:20:17.790 --> 00:20:19.450
Amuro, we did it!

00:20:19.520 --> 00:20:21.080
Thanks to you!

00:20:21.160 --> 00:20:23.820
You were more or less the leader
for this operation, after all.

00:20:23.890 --> 00:20:24.790
Really?

00:20:24.860 --> 00:20:27.020
- Do you really think so?
- Yeah!

00:20:27.100 --> 00:20:29.060
Then what do I get for it?

00:20:31.030 --> 00:20:32.190
That wasn't much!

00:20:32.800 --> 00:20:34.270
Not in front of everyone.

00:20:34.500 --> 00:20:36.270
Congratulations on a successful operation.

00:20:36.670 --> 00:20:37.700
Thank you.

00:20:37.770 --> 00:20:40.870
I couldn't have done it
without the cooperation of everyone.

00:20:41.140 --> 00:20:43.610
- You gave an excellent speech.
- Did I?

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:51.580
What's the matter?

00:20:51.650 --> 00:20:52.620
Nothing.

00:20:53.360 --> 00:20:55.980
Thanks to you, the A.E.U.G.
and Karaba...

00:20:56.060 --> 00:20:58.220
...are filled with excitement
like never before.

00:20:59.190 --> 00:21:00.750
However...

00:21:00.830 --> 00:21:03.530
...I've given up my freedom in exchange.

00:21:03.930 --> 00:21:06.900
- I see your point.
- Yeah.

00:21:07.140 --> 00:21:10.630
But we're trying to take the people
who have remained on Earth to space.

00:21:10.710 --> 00:21:12.370
Such an enormous task can't be done...

00:21:12.440 --> 00:21:14.410
...without at least
one or two human sacrifices.

00:21:14.880 --> 00:21:17.000
So I'm a human sacrifice?

00:21:17.080 --> 00:21:19.480
Maybe human sacrifices run in your family.

00:21:28.420 --> 00:21:29.390
Miss Beltorchika.

00:21:29.930 --> 00:21:31.920
Oh, Kamille. Good job.

00:21:32.460 --> 00:21:35.120
Thank you. You did a good job too.

00:21:37.030 --> 00:21:40.830
Isn't it funny that the two of us
are having such a relaxed conversation?

00:21:40.900 --> 00:21:43.100
You're right.

00:21:45.740 --> 00:21:48.010
Are people destined to end up
hating each other...

00:21:48.080 --> 00:21:49.200
...through misunderstandings?

00:21:49.510 --> 00:21:51.070
No.

00:21:51.150 --> 00:21:54.600
There are people who can envision
what's ahead, and those who can't.

00:21:55.380 --> 00:21:57.680
I realized that if you're too desperate...

00:21:57.750 --> 00:22:00.850
...there are times you'll end up
completely losing that vision.

00:22:01.820 --> 00:22:04.690
- Really?
- See? You're making fun of me.

00:22:04.760 --> 00:22:05.850
No, I'm not!

00:22:05.930 --> 00:22:07.860
I'm moved by your words.

00:22:07.930 --> 00:22:10.660
I think all people can sympathize.

00:22:12.400 --> 00:22:15.530
But that sort of thing takes time.

00:22:15.600 --> 00:22:18.300
Because we're not dealing with
just one or two people.

00:22:18.970 --> 00:22:24.110
However, should a time come when
all people sympathize for one another...

00:22:24.180 --> 00:22:28.120
...I feel that, perhaps we
can even encounter...

00:22:28.180 --> 00:22:30.150
...the people who have passed away.

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.600
Oh, I can't help believing you

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
kanarazu aeru to ano hi kara shinjiteita

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
I've believed we're sure to meet again ever since that day

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
kitto yobiau kokoro ga areba

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
If we have heart, we'll be called together again

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
mugen no Energy yobisamasu

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
Awaken the infinite energy

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
aa kizutsukeau mae ni

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
Before you get hurt

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
dekiru koto sagashite Please

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
Find what you can do...Please

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
nagedasanai de kurushii toki koso

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
Don't throw it away because of this painful age

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
itsuka mita aoi sora wo

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
Until the day we gaze up again

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
kitto anata to miageru hi made

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
at the blue sky we once saw

00:23:47.300 --> 00:23:49.290
Kamille and Char return to space...

00:23:49.360 --> 00:23:53.320
...to meet up with the Argama,
waiting in Earth's orbit.

00:23:54.200 --> 00:23:57.640
However, as they evade
the Titans' attacks...

00:23:57.710 --> 00:24:01.330
...the two sense a strange pressure
from the enemy vessel.

00:24:02.140 --> 00:24:06.840
Next on Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam,
"Reccoa's Shadow".

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:12.440
Next Episode

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:12.440
Reccoa's Shadow

00:24:07.820 --> 00:24:10.350
You will see the tears of time.
